From 620bf5f65e4f127fc4f9daefe153ef8db5e73815 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 22:27:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07165/11362] [outer-loop] fix severe live-path hang in
 ColorBlobSaliencePrior; disable pending re-validation (REQ-ARC-FCP-5591-3)

Found during ARC-AGI-3 submission-prep pre-flight: scripts/kaggle/
arc_local_submission_gate.py --check against the current live scored
config (SUBMITTED_COLOR_BLOB_SALIENCE_ENABLED=True, flipped on 7/7)
returned 0/8 core solves vs the verified baseline's 4/8, with 7 of 8
canonical games timing out at the gate's 115s cap.

Root-caused via a live faulthandler stack trace on a real hung lp85
run (not guesswork): action_tier_rows() already computes the frame's
blob decomposition once at its own top, but then called
self.score(frame, candidate) once per candidate action -- and score()
independently recomputed the SAME full-grid flood-fill from scratch on
every call. Net cost: O(candidates x grid_cells) per next_move(), on a
64x64 grid with thousands of click candidates this is tens of millions
of redundant cell-visits per step -- a de facto hang, not a true
infinite loop, but indistinguishable from one at any realistic budget.

Fixed by threading an optional per-frame blobs/color_counts cache
through score(), computed once in action_tier_rows() and reused across
all candidates. Preserves the exact two-positional-arg score(frame,
candidate) protocol every other action-prior caller in this codebase
depends on. Verified: a previously-hanging lp85 run (180s+, zero
actions) now completes in 25-68s (496 actions, reaches L1, efficiency
exactly matches the gate script's own documented baseline floor
constant).

Even fixed, the flag stays OFF for now: still measurably slower per
action than pre-color-blob-salience baseline, for zero measured
benefit (three follow-on live-path level-up attempts using it, same
day, all returned honest_null). Re-enable only after a fresh
matched-budget A/B under a quiet system state shows a real win.

Updated test_arc_submitted_agent_parity.py to assert the new (correct,
disabled) shipped state instead of asserting the config that was
silently regressing the live path.
